    "body": "> I think GitHub runs all node actions with this separate node version so it works deterministically, regardless what the image has installed.\r\n> \r\n> \r\n> \r\nThanks for reply this！\r\nGitHub distributes Node.js by automatically updating the runner, placing it within an `externals` directory. I believe Gitea should support this approach; whether or not Node.js is bundled directly into Gitea is less critical. Supporting the use of a Node.js instance already present on the host machine would greatly facilitate migrations from GitHub—as well as the reuse of existing CI/CD YAML files and dependencies originally designed for GitHub—while ensuring better compatibility.\r\n\r\n",
    "created_at": "2026-11-06T09:20:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-06T09:20:48Z",
